p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px">=
<span>Just before noon on a holiday weekend earlier this month, while many =
Americans were at the beach, Trump=E2=80=99s social media account roared to=
 life. In what has increasingly become his weekend habit, he unleashed a da=
ylong barrage of posts that put the bully in bully pulpit.</span></p><p sty=
le=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span=
>There were images of Trump intimidating Canada=E2=80=99s prime minister wi=
th a hockey stick. Trump personally bombing enemy targets. Trump patrolling=
 dark streets with killer robots. There were maps showing the United States=
 taking over other countries. There were tributes to himself as =E2=80=9Cth=
e Greatest President of All Time!=E2=80=9D</span></p><p style=3D"font:norma=
l 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The 60 messages=
 posted online over 10 hours and 41 minutes offered a window into Trump=E2=
=80=99s own unique reality. For years, his social media feed was said to be=
 a mirror of his id. But with A.I., it=E2=80=99s become the manifestation o=
f how he wants to be seen in a more visual, visceral way =E2=80=94 as a war=
rior, a conqueror, a historical figure (and a younger, thinner, more muscul=
ar version of himself).</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia=
,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>It=E2=80=99s a measure of how much=
 Trump has changed the nature of the presidency that all this has, to some =
extent, become routine.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia=
,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-weight:700">Flooding=
 the zone</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#=
333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>To his defenders, Trump is a master of baiting h=
is adversaries and getting them to react. =E2=80=9CIt=E2=80=99s called: We =
do a little trolling,=E2=80=9D as he once put it. The more out there the me=
ssage is, the more his supporters cheer. As abnormal as the images that he =
posts are for a president, Trump=E2=80=99s allies argue that they convey a =
raw quality that suits an age of no-holds-barred politics.</span></p><p sty=
le=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span=
>=E2=80=9CThe media and President Trump=E2=80=99s other critics have spent =
more than a decade complaining about his use of social media,=E2=80=9D said=
 Alex Bruesewitz, a former campaign aide. =E2=80=9CThey keep calling it =E2=
=80=98unpresidential,=E2=80=99 but if the president is doing it, it=E2=80=
=99s presidential by definition. I think most Americans appreciate the auth=
entic and transparent way he uses these platforms.=E2=80=8B=E2=80=8B=E2=80=
=8B=E2=80=8B=E2=80=8B=E2=80=8B=E2=80=8B=E2=80=8B=E2=80=8B=E2=80=8B=E2=80=8B=
